  {
   "category": "food_life",
   "desk": "DRINKING",
   "headline": "Korea's drinking culture is changing",
   "hook": "Korea used to drink like champions.\nNow?",
   "characters": {
    "anchor": {
     "head": "../../cast/k_head.png",
     "body": "../../cast/k_body.png",
     "ref": "../../cast/k_ref.png",
     "x": 1290,
     "label": "MASTER K"
    },
    "panel": {
     "head": "../../cast/kangfree_head.png",
     "body": "../../cast/kangfree_body.png",
     "ref": "../../cast/kangfree_ref.png",
     "x": 630,
     "label": "DR. KANGFREE",
     "energy": 1.8,
     "head_ratio": 0.74,
     "shoulders": 500,
     "chin_drop": 0.12
    }
   },
   "screens": {
    "oecd": {
     "card": {
      "title": "ALCOHOL PER PERSON: OECD RANK",
      "stats": [
       {
        "value": "10th",
        "label": "1981"
       },
       {
        "value": "21st",
        "label": "2021"
       }
      ]
     },
     "label": "",
     "credit": "Source: OECD data, via Korean press reports"
    }
   },
   "short": false,
   "name_chips": true,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Hello, world. Welcome back to the Four Eyes Report. Today: how Koreans drink, what they snack on, and what's changing in Korea right now.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_01.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "I'm only here for the snacks!",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_02.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Then let's start with the drinks.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_03.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Let's talk about drinking. By some statistics, Korea once ranked near the top of the world in alcohol per person. Numbers differ by source, but Koreans drank a LOT.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_04.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "I believe it! Korean restaurants never turn their lights off. Twenty-four hours!",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_05.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "But that's changing. In OECD data, Korea has dropped to twenty-first as of 2021, and soju output has fallen three years in a row.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_06.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "k_screen",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "oecd"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Wait, soju is down?! Soju is SO hot overseas right now!",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_07.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Koreans still drink. Just not like before. It went from a marathon to a brisk walk.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_08.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "And the taste changed too. First everyone loved wine, and now whisky is the cool one, right?",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_09.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Yes. \"A bottle of soju for the lady at the next table!\" is out. \"A glass of whisky\" has more style.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_10.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Smooth. Very smooth.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_11.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "The biggest change is the honsul bar. Koreans used to drink in big groups. Now younger people enjoy a good drink alone.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_12.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "But everyone there is single, and hot, so it turns into a place to meet people!",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_13.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "You sit alone, you use a nickname, and you talk only if you want to.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_14.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Okay, next time I'm in Korea, I'm going!",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_15.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "One warning. There's no age limit. But Korea has \"ip-ppaen\": getting turned away at the door. Officially, never. In a bar full of young people, you can feel it.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_16.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Feel what?",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_17.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Every head turning to say, \"Sir... are you lost?\"",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_18.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Don't worry, Master K. I'll vouch for you at the door.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_19.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Thank you. I'll just drink at home.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_20.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "category": "food_life",
   "desk": "STREET FOOD",
   "headline": "Bunsik: the street snack that went global",
   "hook": "Koreans are shocked\nthis street food went global.",
   "characters": {
    "anchor": {
     "head": "../../cast/k_head.png",
     "body": "../../cast/k_body.png",
     "ref": "../../cast/k_ref.png",
     "x": 1290,
     "label": "MASTER K"
    },
    "panel": {
     "head": "../../cast/kangfree_head.png",
     "body": "../../cast/kangfree_body.png",
     "ref": "../../cast/kangfree_ref.png",
     "x": 630,
     "label": "DR. KANGFREE",
     "energy": 1.8,
     "head_ratio": 0.74,
     "shoulders": 500,
     "chin_drop": 0.12
    },
    "chef": {
     "head": "../../cast/chef_head.png",
     "body": "../../cast/chef_body.png",
     "ref": "../../cast/chef_ref.png",
     "x": 2700,
     "label": "CHEF CLAMSAY",
     "shoulders": 520,
     "white_lens": true,
     "head_ratio": 0.74,
     "chin_drop": 0.16,
     "mood": "frown"
    }
   },
   "screens": {
    "kimbap": {
     "image": "../../assets/stock/ep02/kimbap_2.jpg",
     "label": "KIMBAP",
     "credit": "Photo: manda_wong (BY 2.0)"
    },
    "street": {
     "image": "../../assets/stock/ep02/street_food.jpg",
     "label": "KOREAN STREET FOOD",
     "credit": "Photo: JDKEUP (BY 2.0)"
    },
    "tteok_after": {
     "image": "../../assets/stock/ep02/tteokbokki_after.jpg",
     "label": "TTEOKBOKKI",
     "credit": "Photo: Jon Åslund (BY 2.0)"
    },
    "tteok_chilli": {
     "image": "../../assets/stock/ep02/rice_cake_chilli.jpg",
     "label": "TTEOK ON A STICK",
     "credit": "Photo: angusf (BY 2.0)"
    },
    "tteok_street": {
     "image": "../../assets/stock/ep02/tteokbokki_street.jpg",
     "label": "TTEOKBOKKI",
     "credit": "Photo: Ten-ele-ven (BY 2.0)"
    }
   },
   "short": false,
   "name_chips": true,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "chef",
     "text": "Did somebody say \"home\"? I brought snacks. Do you know bunsik? Korean snack food. And here's the thing: Koreans are shocked that it's popular overseas.",
     "audio": "audio/v5_calm/ep02_21.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      2700,
      470,
      1.3
     ],
     "ease": 0.12,
     "cam_id": "chef",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Really? It's delicious! Of course it's popular. I don't understand why they don't understand!",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_22.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Because bunsik is classic street food. Spicy, salty, sweet, and you can find it almost anywhere in Korea.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_23.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "k_screen",
     "push": false,
     "screen": [
      "street",
      "kimbap"
     ],
     "screen_split": [
      0.45
     ]
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Wait. Almost anywhere? Like, every corner?",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_24.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Every corner. And it's cheap.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_25.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "k_screen",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "tteok_chilli"
    },
    {
     "who": "chef",
     "text": "Mostly students. After school, they pool their allowance and share one plate of tteokbokki.",
     "audio": "audio/v5_calm/ep02_26.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      2700,
      470,
      1.3
     ],
     "ease": 0.12,
     "cam_id": "chef",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "So it's a group project. And everyone actually does their part: eating.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_27.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "So Koreans see a corner-stand snack become a global hit, and they're surprised. It's like Americans finding out the whole world loves a gas station hot dog.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_28.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "k_screen",
     "push": false,
     "screen": [
      "tteok_street",
      "tteok_after"
     ],
     "screen_split": [
      0.45
     ]
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "I bet it's the K-dramas. Everyone watches them overseas, and the food looks amazing.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_29.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "chef",
     "text": "Part of it, yes. Someone slurps ramen in a drama, and a thousand people run to buy ramen.",
     "audio": "audio/v5_calm/ep02_30.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      2700,
      470,
      1.3
     ],
     "ease": 0.12,
     "cam_id": "chef",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "K-drama is an advertisement money can't buy.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_31.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "chef",
     "text": "Culture spreads, more people touch it, and then everyone chooses their own taste.",
     "audio": "audio/v5_calm/ep02_32.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      2700,
      470,
      1.3
     ],
     "ease": 0.12,
     "cam_id": "chef",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Mine is tteokbokki. Spicy, chewy, and I can't stop.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_33.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "chef",
     "text": "Careful. Last time we ate spicy, one of us died.",
     "audio": "audio/v5_calm/ep02_34.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      2700,
      470,
      1.3
     ],
     "ease": 0.12,
     "cam_id": "chef",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "And we never found out who!",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_35.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "...Moving on.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_36.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "One last question. Do bunsik shops have ip-ppaen too?",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_37.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "chef",
     "text": "Seriously?",
     "audio": "audio/v5_calm/ep02_38.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      2700,
      470,
      1.3
     ],
     "ease": 0.12,
     "cam_id": "chef",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "The only face control at a bunsik shop is the face you make when someone takes the last fish cake.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_39.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "chef",
     "text": "I remember that face.",
     "audio": "audio/v5_calm/ep02_40.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      2700,
      470,
      1.3
     ],
     "ease": 0.12,
     "cam_id": "chef",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "...Sorry about the fish cake.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_41.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Enough food. Let's talk about how young Koreans are feeling. Spoiler: bored.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_42.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    }
   ]
  },
