    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Korea has a word for the moment a hobby suddenly stops being fun. \"Taegi.\"",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_43.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "A word for that? Like, \"I used to love running, now I hate my shoes\"?",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_44.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Exactly. Golf-taegi. Running-taegi. Reading-taegi. Add it to anything that stopped being fun.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_45.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "chef",
     "text": "Cooking-taegi.",
     "audio": "audio/v5_calm/ep02_46.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      2700,
      470,
      1.3
     ],
     "ease": 0.12,
     "cam_id": "chef",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Chef! You can't have cooking-taegi!",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_47.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "chef",
     "text": "Only for one lunch. I'm better now.",
     "audio": "audio/v5_calm/ep02_48.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      2700,
      470,
      1.3
     ],
     "ease": 0.12,
     "cam_id": "chef",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "A Seoul trend forecaster even named \"the age of boredom\" the first trend of 2027. Too much stimulation, so nothing feels interesting.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_49.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "k_screen",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "boredom"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "So what do bored Koreans do?",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_50.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "They squeeze things. \"Mallang-i,\" soft squishy toys. One type jumped seven hundred seventy-four percent in a single month.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_51.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "k_screen",
     "push": false,
     "screen": [
      "squish_ai",
      "squish"
     ],
     "screen_split": [
      0.45
     ]
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Seven hundred seventy-four percent?!",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_52.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "And wax-crushing balls. You crush the hard shell with your hand. Sales jumped five hundred percent.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_53.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "chef",
     "text": "So it's cracking an egg without the egg.",
     "audio": "audio/v5_calm/ep02_54.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      2700,
      470,
      1.3
     ],
     "ease": 0.12,
     "cam_id": "chef",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "About half of the people surveyed, aged thirteen to fifty-nine, had tried something like it.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_55.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "k_screen",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "tactile"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "I tried one at the airport. It's squishy. It's very squishy.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_56.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "That's your review?",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_57.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Five stars.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_58.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "And I heard about lucky turtles!",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_59.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Tiny turtles, smaller than a fingernail. Young Koreans carry them for luck in love, school, work, even investing.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_60.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "k_screen",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "turtle_ai"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Investing?! My portfolio needs a turtle.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_61.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Slow and steady. Honestly, that's good financial advice.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_62.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "chef",
     "text": "Is the turtle edible?",
     "audio": "audio/v5_calm/ep02_63.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      2700,
      470,
      1.3
     ],
     "ease": 0.12,
     "cam_id": "chef",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "No. Chef.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_64.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Speaking of turtles: I heard even running is slowing down in Korea.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_65.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "True. Seoul held a run called \"My Pace Morning.\" You finish at your own speed.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_66.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "k_screen",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "run_ai"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "A race where nobody loses?",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_67.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Nobody wins, nobody checks the clock. Maybe that's the cure for running-taegi.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_68.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "chef",
     "text": "I'll be at the finish line. With snacks.",
     "audio": "audio/v5_calm/ep02_69.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      2700,
      470,
      1.3
     ],
     "ease": 0.12,
     "cam_id": "chef",
     "push": false
    }
   ]
  },
  {
