    },
    "jeon": {
     "image": "../../assets/stock/ep02/pa_jeon.jpg",
     "label": "JEON (PAN-FRIED PANCAKE)",
     "credit": "Photo: Maggie Hoffman (BY 2.0)"
    },
    "rites": {
     "card": {
      "title": "HOUSEHOLDS PLANNING ANCESTRAL RITES",
      "stats": [
       {
        "value": 74.4,
        "decimals": 1,
        "suffix": "%",
        "label": "2016"
       },
       {
        "value": 27.3,
        "decimals": 1,
        "suffix": "%",
        "label": "2026"
       }
      ]
     },
     "label": "",
     "credit": "Source: Seoul Economic Daily, 2026"
    }
   },
   "short": false,
   "name_chips": true,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "One more change. Chuseok. Korean Thanksgiving, the biggest family holiday of the year.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_70.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Everyone goes home, eats a mountain of food, and does the ancestral rites, right?",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_71.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Less and less. In 2016, about seventy-four percent of households planned ancestral rites. As of 2026, about twenty-seven percent.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_72.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "k_screen",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "rites"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "From three-quarters to one-quarter!",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_73.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "And forty-three percent planned only a family gathering. No rites, no grave visits.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_74.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "k_screen",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "family"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Some families don't even go home. They book a hotel in Seoul. A \"hotel vacation.\"",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_75.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Because the stress isn't the food. It's the questions.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_76.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "k_screen",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "hotel_ai"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "\"When are you getting married? Do you have a job? How much do you make?\"",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_77.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Three questions. Same relatives. Every year.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_78.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "I have a strategy. When an aunt asks, \"When are you getting married?\" I say, \"Have you tried the jeon?\"",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_79.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Jeon. Pan-fried treats, a Chuseok classic. A secret weapon.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_80.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "k_screen",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "jeon"
    },
    {
     "who": "chef",
     "text": "Works every time. A full mouth asks no questions.",
     "audio": "audio/v5_calm/ep02_81.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      2700,
      470,
      1.3
     ],
     "ease": 0.12,
     "cam_id": "chef",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Then the cousin comes up. \"Your cousin just got promoted.\"",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_82.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "There is always a cousin. Always perfect.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_83.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "I'm a doctor! And I still hear, \"But have you met someone nice?\"",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_84.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Doctor, even doctors lose to relatives.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_85.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "chef",
     "text": "I just bring more jeon.",
     "audio": "audio/v5_calm/ep02_86.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      2700,
      470,
      1.3
     ],
     "ease": 0.12,
     "cam_id": "chef",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "So the new Chuseok is a hotel, a movie, and silence?",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_87.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Not exactly. Most people still gather. The ritual is changing. The reunion stays.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_88.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "And the food? Please tell me the food survived.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_89.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "It did. Songpyeon, half-moon rice cakes steamed on pine needles, are still a Chuseok classic.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_90.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "chef",
     "text": "Finally, my department. Pine needles. The whole kitchen smells like a forest.",
     "audio": "audio/v5_calm/ep02_91.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      2700,
      470,
      1.3
     ],
     "ease": 0.12,
     "cam_id": "chef",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Even Chuseok has a skip button now.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_92.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Just don't skip the call to Grandma.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_93.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "So here's my take. Korea changes fast. But people still want the same thing: someone to share a plate with, a drink with, a holiday with. Even if the holiday is in a hotel.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_94.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Tell us in the comments: which Korean habit confuses you most?",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_95.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Subscribe, and we'll see you next Friday. Stay curious. Keep your lenses clean.",
     "audio": "audio/v5/ep02_96.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}